  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In May 2026, Deputy NIST Director Craig Burkhardt invited technically capable organizations to join the NIST AI Consortium and said NIST was seeking to expand AI measurement efforts by harnessing the broader community’s interests and capabilities. In March 2026, he said the CAISI-GSA partnership would enable federal agencies to adopt AI in ways that help the American people and expressed excitement about advancing AI in support of the Trump Administration’s innovation vision. In December 2025, while Acting NIST Director, he said his goal was to remove barriers to American AI innovation and accelerate the application of AI technologies around the world. Also in December 2025, he described a new MITRE agreement as focused on helping U.S. companies make high-value products more efficiently, meet market demands, and catalyze discovery and commercialization of new technologies and devices.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s5",
    "s3",
    "s6",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
